  <text>
      <body>
        <p><pb edRef="Laud610" n="fol.124"/><cb edRef="Laud610" n="fol.124ra"/>do boí ac <name type="person" nymRef="F64">Fi<expan>n</expan>d</name>’, ar <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissī<expan>n</expan></name>, ‘.i. <name type="person" nymRef="U2">Ūai<expan>n</expan>e i<expan>n</expan>ge<expan>n</expan> Moduir<expan>n</expan>d</name> ⁊ tuc <name type="person" nymRef="F64">Fi<expan>n</expan>d</name> éra tochmairc furri ara i<expan>m</expan>mat d’ilrachtaib a téiged-si ūair ní raibe bethadach nā téighed-si [i] richt ⁊ tāngad<expan>ur</expan> i<expan>n</expan>d ḟīan<expan>n</expan> laithe n-ǣ<expan>n</expan> a<expan>r</expan>i<expan>n</expan> ca<expan>r</expan>n<expan>n</expan> ōs chi<expan>n</expan>d i<expan>n</expan> locha si<expan>n</expan> ⁊ tāinic in fīad amach a<expan>r</expan>i<expan>n</expan> loch ⁊ do lenamar-ne ari<expan>n</expan> loch hé ⁊ do ēirig i<expan>n</expan> pēist dūind ⁊ do ma<expan>r</expan>b <expan>cét</expan> cú ⁊ <expan>cét</expan> fer accai<expan>n</expan>d ⁊ is an<expan>n</expan>sin do īa<expan>r</expan>faig <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Caīl<expan>ti</expan></name> do Ḟi<expan>n</expan>d: “in li<expan>n</expan>d tuitfis in pēist ⁊ mas ed co cuirmis rīa ⁊ co ṅdīghlamais a<expan>r</expan> muint<expan>ir</expan> furri?”.</p>
<p>⁊ tuc <name type="person" nymRef="F64">Find</name> a ordai<expan>n</expan> fā déd fis ⁊ ro faillsiged fír fāistine dó ⁊ adubairt in laīd:</p>

<p xml:id="Laud610_poem62"><lg type="quatrain" n="1"><l>“<name type="place" nymRef="g19"><hi rend="decor">Gl</hi>end Rois Enaig</name> bid fīr dam</l>
<l>bid bind guth cluic an<expan>n</expan> bīaid tan</l>
<l>gé beth fó damaib rūada</l>
<l>robsat ili a a<expan>r</expan>dbūada.</l></lg>
    
<lg type="quatrain" n="2"><l><hi rend="decor">R</hi>o gab i<expan>n</expan> doi<expan>n</expan>end dubad</l>
<l>nī soinend <expan>acht</expan> a<expan>r</expan> selaib</l>
<l>do gab i<expan>n</expan> tal<expan>am</expan> trochull</l>
<l>do gab cochull cend n-enaig.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="3"><l><hi rend="decor">E</hi>nach fēi<expan>n</expan>de fadb fulaig</l>
<l>i<expan>m-</expan>rulaig ga<expan>r</expan>b re <expan>con</expan>aib</l>
<l>sīat srotha, elta enaig,</l>
<l>rīa<expan>n</expan> t<expan>r</expan>egai<expan>n</expan>, terchtha t<expan>r</expan>ogai<expan>n</expan>.</l></lg>

<lg type="quatrain" n="4"><l><pb xml:id="Stokes_p.69"/><hi rend="decor"></hi><hi rend="decor">C</hi>rotholl fēin<expan>n</expan>e, fūath curraig,</l>
<l>ōs duillib rūada ri<expan>n</expan>dib</l>
<l>sceō gaīthi ceó ta<expan>r</expan> ri<expan>n</expan>dib</l>
<l>ōs rengaib leab<expan>r</expan>a a<expan>r</expan> li<expan>n</expan>dib.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="5"><l><hi rend="decor">C</hi>osc<expan>r</expan>ach at-chiū-sa an muirbich</l>
<l>rosc dercai<expan>n</expan>,<note><p>Recte: <expan>rosc drecain</expan> ‘eye of a dragon’? Cf. Lis. rosc d<expan>r</expan>eacoin; R rus-geoghui<expan>n</expan>; F rosg dregai<expan>n.</expan>,</p></note> b<expan>r</expan>āth tar buidnib,</l>
<l>tǣbúai<expan>n</expan>e taithnem taidlech</l>
<l>bīaid Cǽ<expan>m</expan>gi<expan>n</expan> ’gā <expan>m</expan>bīa cuibrech.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="6"><l><hi rend="decor">M</hi>uirbech lon<expan>n</expan> <name type="place" nymRef="l48">Locha hEnaig</name></l>
<l>ton<expan>n</expan> ’na degaid ad-<expan>r</expan>aigi</l>
<l>sissi ac slaidhi na féi<expan>n</expan>de</l>
<l>óig na fēi<expan>n</expan>de ’gā slaide.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="7"><l><hi rend="decor">D</hi>eich ṁblī<expan>adna</expan> a<expan>r</expan> dā blī<expan>adain</expan></l>
<l>a hocht, rīagail ar relaig,</l>
<l>a<expan>r</expan> dā <expan>cét</expan> dēg, sét saíre,</l>
<l>g<expan>us</expan>i<expan>n</expan> aí<expan>n</expan>e ro genair.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="8"><l><name type="place" nymRef="l48"><hi rend="decor">L</hi>och nEnaig</name>, adhba elad,</l>
<l>scīth cen ḟīanna ’na ḟarrud</l>
<l>tāilgi<expan>n</expan>d <expan>con-</expan>tagfat ui<expan>m</expan>e</l>
<l>badh bi<expan>n</expan>de chanfat aille.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="9"><l><name type="place" nymRef="l48"><hi rend="decor">L</hi>och nEnaid</name>, adhba ela,</l>
<l>di<expan>n</expan>d ṁbera itir dā mbroi<expan>n</expan>e</l>
<l>enach t<expan>r</expan>ogai<expan>n</expan>, blaí théite,</l>
<l>ōtá in chéiti co ’raili.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="10"><l><name type="place" nymRef="g19"><hi rend="decor">G</hi>lend Enaig</name> it<expan>ir</expan> dā tṡlīab</l>
<l>iss é is áille at-con<expan>n</expan>arcc rīam</l>
<l>abhand dā loch a<expan>r</expan>a lār</l>
<l>iss é lán don leith anīa<expan>r</expan>.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="11"><l>><hi rend="decor">B</hi>idh adhba ailithrech ūa<expan>r</expan></l>
<l>bid adba t<expan>r</expan>én ⁊ t<expan>r</expan>ūag</l>
<l>bid adhnacht rīg cend a cen<expan>n</expan></l>
<l>ticfa <name type="person" nymRef="C3">Cǽ<expan>m</expan>gei<expan>n</expan></name> issin ṅglen<expan>n</expan>.</l>
<l>Glen<expan>n</expan>”.</l></lg></p>

<p><hi rend="decor">N</hi>í héitir a i<expan>n</expan>dissi<expan>n</expan> nā a aisnēis neoch ro i<expan>n</expan>disseta<expan>r</expan> do dēnam dóib féi<expan>n</expan> do mōrgnī<expan>m</expan>aib gaile ⁊ gaiscid ⁊ do maithib na féi<expan>n</expan>e re tǽb dindsenchais ca<expan>ch</expan> cnuic ⁊ ca<expan>ch</expan> ḟerai<expan>n</expan>d ro ḟīa<expan>r</expan>faigeta<expan>r</expan> fir <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name> díb.</p>
        
<p>I<hi rend="decor">S</hi> an<expan>n</expan>si<expan>n</expan> tāi<expan>n</expan>ic <name type="person" nymRef="T6">Trénbrugaid m<expan>a</expan>c Trēin</name> .i. flaithbriugaid <expan>cét</expan>ach co<expan>m</expan>ramach do ríg Ēir<expan>enn</expan> .i. t<expan>r</expan>ī .l. f<expan>er</expan> mōr i<expan>n</expan>a ḟa<expan>rr</expan>ad ⁊ faiderān fírgor<expan>m</expan> i<expan>m</expan> ca<expan>ch</expan> fer díb ⁊ lēi<expan>n</expan>ti lígdha lángela u<expan>m</expan>pu ⁊ t<expan>r</expan>ī .l. gaballorg ina lámaib. ⁊ ro ben<expan>n</expan>aiged<expan>ur</expan> do rí <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name> ⁊ f<expan>r</expan>eg<expan>r</expan>ais i<expan>n</expan> rí īat.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">A</hi>tá fleg mōr acai<expan>n</expan>d duit, a ríg’, a<expan>r</expan> sīat, ‘.i. deich fichid dabach do midh ⁊ deich .xx. dabach do chuir<expan>m</expan> glai<expan>n</expan> gabāltaig <expan>con</expan>a dǣithi<expan>n</expan> do bíadaib ila<expan>r</expan>da écsamlaib leó’.</p>
        
<p>⁊ tucsat i<expan>n</expan> bīad ⁊ i<expan>n</expan> li<expan>n</expan>d leó don ríg.</p>
        
<p><hi rend="decor">ET</hi> do ḟīa<expan>r</expan>faig rí <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name> <name type="person" nymRef="O2">d’Oissī<expan>n</expan></name>: ‘i<expan>n</expan> a n-ǣ<expan>n</expan>tech re maithib <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name> rachaisi <expan>nó</expan> i<expan>n</expan> tech óil ⁊ aībni<expan>us</expan>a a<expan>r</expan> leith bes accaib?’.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">A</hi><expan>r</expan> cuit bíd ⁊ lenda dūind <cb edRef="Laud610" n="fol.124rb"/>ar leith’, arsi <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissī<expan>n</expan></name>, ‘ūai<expan>r</expan> ní lu<expan>cht</expan> co<expan>m</expan>díne nā co<expan>m</expan>ai<expan>m</expan>sire dūi<expan>n</expan>d na daíne anois’.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">C</hi>á lín atáthi?’, a<expan>r</expan> rīg Ēir<expan>enn</expan>.</p>
        
<p>‘Dā nǣnb<expan>ur</expan>’, ar <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissīn</name>, ‘.i. nōnbur dam-sa ⁊ nǣnb<expan>ur</expan> dom’ <pb xml:id="Stokes_p.70"/>cho<expan>m</expan>alta do <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Chaīlti</name>’.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">F</hi>iche dabach <expan>con</expan>a ndǣithi<expan>n</expan> bíd dōib’, a<expan>r</expan> rí <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name>.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">M</hi>aith, a ríg’, a<expan>r</expan> <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Caīlti</name>, ‘nā cut<expan>r</expan>umaig-siu si<expan>n</expan>d do biud <expan>nó</expan> do li<expan>n</expan>d chaīchi. Ūair i<expan>n</expan> tan do-berthea deich ndabcha damh-sa .xxx. dabach [...] chóir<note><p>Stain in MS; space for approximately 2-3 letters.</p></note> <name type="person" nymRef="O2">d’Oissī<expan>n</expan></name>’.</p>
        
<p>⁊ ro chaithed<expan>ur</expan> i<expan>n</expan>d adhaig si<expan>n</expan> co subach sobrónach co tāi<expan>n</expan>ic lā <expan>con</expan>a lānṡoillsi gan uresbaid bíd nā dighi forro.</p>
        
<p><hi rend="decor">O</hi>c<expan>us</expan> do cuired a phupall ta<expan>r</expan> rīg <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name> issi<expan>n</expan> tulaig thon<expan>n</expan>glais i<expan>n</expan> lá si<expan>n</expan> ⁊ nír’ léiced ach rídamna issi<expan>n</expan> pupaill ⁊ tāi<expan>n</expan>ic Pāt<expan>r</expan>aic <expan>con</expan>a chléirchib issi<expan>n</expan> da<expan>r</expan>na leth don phupaill ⁊ nír’ léiced <expan>acht</expan> esgob ⁊ saca<expan>r</expan>t ⁊ mac ochta Rīg Ni<expan>m</expan>e ⁊ Tal<expan>man</expan> issi<expan>n</expan> leith i rroibe <name type="person" nymRef="P1">Pāt<expan>raic</expan></name>. <hi rend="decor">S</hi>uidhis <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissīn</name> i fīadnaissi <name type="person" nymRef="P1"><expan>Pátraic</expan></name> ⁊ <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Caīlti</name> i fīadnaisi rīg <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name>.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">C</hi>īa accaib as si<expan>n</expan>e?’, ar rí <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name>.</p>
        
<p>‘Missi’, a<expan>r</expan> <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Caīlti</name>, ‘ūair .x. mblī<expan>adna</expan> .xx. dobo tṡlān dam i<expan>n</expan> tan rucad <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissīn</name> ⁊ .uíí. mblī<expan>adna</expan> déc dó am’ leapaid-sea ⁊ as mo thigh ro gab fēi<expan>n</expan>d ⁊ foiri<expan>n</expan>d’.</p>

<p><hi rend="decor">IS an<expan>n</expan>sin</hi> do ḟīarfaig rīg <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēirenn</name>: ‘cá lí<expan>n</expan> do rígaib <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name> leis a tucad feran<expan>n</expan> don ḟēind?’.</p>
        
<p>Freg<expan>r</expan>ais <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Caīlti</name> si<expan>n</expan> ōr do boí a ḟis aice .i. ‘<hi rend="decor">r</hi>īg ro gab<expan>us</expan>d<expan>ur</expan> <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>inn</expan></name> .i. <name type="person" nymRef="F21">F<expan>er</expan>adach Fechtnach</name> ⁊ da bād<expan>ur</expan> dā m<expan>a</expan>c aici .i. <name type="person" nymRef="T15">Tūathal</name> ⁊ <name type="person" nymRef="F46">Fīacha</name> a n-an<expan>m</expan>a<expan>nn</expan>a ⁊ fūai<expan>r</expan> <name type="person" nymRef="F21">Feradhach</name> bás ⁊ do roi<expan>n</expan>dset a dā m<expan>a</expan>c éire eturru .i. seóit ⁊ maī<expan>n</expan>e ⁊ i<expan>n</expan>dm<expan>us</expan>a ⁊ būara ⁊ bóthāi<expan>n</expan>te, a failgi ⁊ a fornasca, a ndūinte ⁊ a ndi<expan>n</expan>gna ⁊ a <expan>n</expan>degbailti don<note><p>MS: don don.</p>
    
</note> darna fer. <hi rend="decor">A</hi> halla ⁊ a hi<expan>n</expan>db<expan>er</expan>a, a mes ⁊ a mōrthorad ⁊ a héicned[a] āille eoch<expan>ur</expan>b<expan>rec</expan>a ⁊ a fīadach don ḟir aile’.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">C</hi>āit a ndern<expan>n</expan>sat i<expan>n</expan> roi<expan>n</expan>d sin?’, a<expan>r</expan> rí <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name>.</p>
<p>‘I<expan>m</expan>mon cnoc so ara fuilmid i<expan>n</expan>a<expan>r</expan> suidhe do roi<expan>n</expan>dset dā m<expan>a</expan>c [in] rīg <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>inn</expan></name><note><p>Cf. above (l. 2472): do roi<expan>n</expan>dset a dā m<expan>a</expan>c éire eturru.</p>
</note> eturru’.</p>
        
<p>‘<hi rend="decor">N</hi>í samlaithi i<expan>n</expan> dā roi<expan>n</expan>d sin’, a<expan>r</expan> maithe fer <name type="place" nymRef="e6">nĒir<expan>enn</expan></name>.</p>

<p>‘Cé díb roi<expan>n</expan>d bod ferr lib-si?’, a<expan>r</expan> <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissī<expan>n</expan></name>, ‘.i. a fleda ⁊ a tighi ⁊ a maithi<expan>us</expan> a<expan>r</expan>chena issi<expan>n</expan> da<expan>r</expan>na roi<expan>n</expan>d dīb a feda ⁊ a fāssaigi, a selg ⁊ a fīadach issi<expan>n</expan> roi<expan>n</expan>d aili’.</p>
        
<p>‘I<expan>n</expan> roi<expan>n</expan>d ba messa díb’, a<expan>r</expan> <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Caīlti</name>, ‘iss í ba ferr li<expan>n</expan>de’.</p>

<p>‘Ráid ⁊ i<expan>n</expan>dis a ḟíri<expan>n</expan>de siūt, a <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Chaīlti</name>’, ar <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissī<expan>n</expan></name>. <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissī<expan>n</expan></name> c<expan>e</expan>c<expan>init</expan>:</p>

<p xml:id="Laud610_poem63"><lg type="quatrain" n="1"><l>‘<hi rend="decor">Rāid, a</hi> <name type="person" nymRef="C6">Chaīlti</name>, cid dīa fuil</l>
<l>mōr eōl<expan>us</expan> ré īa<expan>r</expan>faigid?</l>
<l>cētroi<expan>n</expan>d <name type="place" nymRef="e6">Ēir<expan>enn</expan></name>, l<expan>et</expan>h a<expan>r</expan> leth,</l>
<l>do cach c<expan>r</expan>īch fil u<expan>m</expan> <name type="place" nymRef="u3">Uisnech</name>’.</l></lg>

<lg type="quatrain" n="2"><l><pb xml:id="Stokes_p.71"/> ‘<hi rend="decor">C</hi>īa do-rat f<expan>er</expan>ann don ḟēind?</l>
<l>I<expan>n</expan>d ab<expan>r</expan>ai f<expan>r</expan>iu<expan>m</expan>, a <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oisséin</name>?</l>
<l>Cīa ro scar re gilla<expan>cht</expan> <expan>c</expan>h<expan>on</expan>?</l>
<l>Cīa ros-dīl fā thūar<expan>us</expan>dul?</l></lg>

<lg type="quatrain" n="3"><l><hi rend="decor">M</hi>eadbair lem i<expan>n</expan> ní dīa fuil</l>
<l>a m<expan>ei</expan>c <name type="person" nymRef="I17">I<expan>n</expan>gi<expan>n</expan>e in D<expan>eir</expan>g</name> drui<expan>n</expan></l>
<l>ó ro lessaig <name type="person" nymRef="F46">Fīacha</name> i<expan>n</expan> féi<expan>n</expan>d</l>
<l>coro athrigissi, a <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oisséi<expan>n</expan></name>.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="4"><l><hi rend="decor">D</hi>eich mblī<expan>adna</expan> do ḟlaithi<expan>us</expan> maith</l>
<l>duit-siu, a <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Ossī<expan>n</expan></name>, a ardḟlaith</l>
<l>ó r<expan>us</expan>-brég <name type="person" nymRef="F17">Fathad</name> i<expan>n</expan> féind</l>
<l>co rus-t<expan>r</expan>éigset tú, a <name type="person" nymRef="O2">Oissēi<expan>n</expan></name>.</l></lg>
  
<lg type="quatrain" n="5"><l><hi rend="decor">D</hi>egm<expan>a</expan>c <name type="person" n="F21">F<expan>er</expan>adaig</name> da<expan>r</expan> li<expan>m</expan></l>
<l>da<expan>r</expan>bo cho<expan>m</expan>ainm <name type="person" nymRef="F46">Fīacha Fi<expan>n</expan>d</name></l>
<l>><name type="person" nymRef="E50">Eithne i<expan>n</expan>gen Dāi<expan>r</expan>e Duib</name></l>
<l>rob’ í i<expan>n</expan> mōr-rīgu a māthai<expan>r</expan>.</l></lg>

